     "label": null,
     "prompt": "If $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=3x^2-4x$, and $y=3$ when $x=1$, find $y$ as a function of $x$.",
     "answer": {
      "short": "$y=x^3-2x^2+4$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\int(3x^2-4x)\\,dx\\\\&=x^3-2x^2+C\\end{align*}$$\nWhen $x=1$, $y=3$:\n$$\\begin{align*}3&=1-2+C\\\\C&=4\\end{align*}$$\nSo $y=x^3-2x^2+4$."
     },
